{"title":"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Equation_Algorithm)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Equation Algorithm)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the addition shown below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are distinct digits. How many different values are possible for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f247ec6fe2d36c608337f8763645addb01b26338.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}{cccccc}&amp;A&amp;B&amp;B&amp;C&amp;B\\\\ +&amp;B&amp;C&amp;A&amp;D&amp;A\\\\ \\hline &amp;D&amp;B&amp;D&amp;D&amp;D\\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34a23755316a95d6f98babbf3842eb4425f5905b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the first column, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/8229ace7da47e119dd86eb7278ced3b6cc4dd2ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" /> because it yields a single digit answer.  From the fourth column, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169e715676d726e920ca79d2e53b05192ddedc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C+D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85aac914361efb48aaa13187304c1c5bdfef0589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />.  We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fd98f4d430c80047b5c62fcdbda50ebe09325dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B = D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, the number of values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> can take is equal to the number of possible sums less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> that can be formed by adding two distinct natural numbers.  Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18428217dcd07944b2adbebcafd0978587a770a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, and letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842a1dcf90ca82c69b6f6eac7e5293d91175188c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=2,3,4,5,6,7,8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f382073856e4df5d26848d12cc1b47ef6cb9d2a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D = 3,4,5,6,7,8,9 \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7}\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First of all, focus on the second column from right to left. If we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/9/7296755ef63523ef0ed2e997caae100445bbb44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/2072bfcb168c0254116c78263126d900d7e7c956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C+D=D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> will be easily satisfied. Hence, we will first try setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThe addition has become\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d21d253c465567e2497871aa551a72cf60cc12ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}{cccccc}&amp;A&amp;B&amp;B&amp;0&amp;B\\\\ +&amp;B&amp;0&amp;A&amp;D&amp;A\\\\ \\hline &amp;D&amp;B&amp;D&amp;D&amp;D\\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIt is now in a very regular form —— Two columns are automatically satisfied, and the other three columns are all in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca40b0cad654c5ba05b678aa8eb94dfc972947f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B=D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />. As long as we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca40b0cad654c5ba05b678aa8eb94dfc972947f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B=D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />, all the five columns will be satisfied.\n</p><p><br />\nSetting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18428217dcd07944b2adbebcafd0978587a770a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842a1dcf90ca82c69b6f6eac7e5293d91175188c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=2,3,4,5,6,7,8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />, we can construct any value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de4eb730cf77a9992a5a4a50a92b49e33aae3848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,4,5,6,7,8,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />. But what about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe8a942854c711340544034d27acab17e02a990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=0,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><br />\nWe can actually prove that they are all impossible. We now dive into the fifth column from right to left.\n</p><p><br />\nIf there is no carrying, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca40b0cad654c5ba05b678aa8eb94dfc972947f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B=D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />. If carrying occurs, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4f4bd01c4c2d9372b25b1f394509acc0679745a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B+1=D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" />. No matter whether carrying takes place or not, we have the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a40151c105dc02fae44deb1519edd6510ee04b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B\\leq{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f92f2b19827ba2b3e6f39e36a629d25cad9ad8e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=0$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89c2ffd8064347af496c30b54a1684431f70cb3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=B=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" />. This is a contradiction as all the digits are distinct. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c48a8e1afba0b0df47d1c148ed647de6b107970c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D\\neq{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe2fac3dab3afa8b1d414ed5eadeba8ec1aaf08f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/539fcc08371d264b019b31b259190d25d82473e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B\\leq{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />. One of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has to be zero.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Lemma:</i>\n</p><p><br />\nNeither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> can be zero.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Proof:</i>\n</p><p><br />\nFocus on the first column from right to left.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f44a5278f9f07028b5386312e86885738ffec92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=0$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85ac5a80702d56577d4138e1ad27b0ed48ac3d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=D$\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" />. The digits are no longer distinct.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/33535d13e10f27c6657f5795ecb46f5c415ad539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/0/160bf1d3037daacf022becc3935d530ab8943e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. The digits are also no longer distinct.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/b/9ab2b158359c752a5efb35dcfcf31d51397d5cd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D\\neq{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5fa11a4ce3ea4f313886ce680b3bde00e33bf52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=2$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03ba131d1c3d103065f778bcda370ccba62c36d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B\\leq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13e215f3781b2866a910fa12f25f97a07080e4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)\\neq(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" /> as the digits are distinct. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff7fd15c9fbe832dfad714d1eeb078c4d87a36c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)=(0,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c67f1e6c098104b1cb8f1cdd6bb16f689ac3e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, which both involve one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> being zero.\n</p><p><br />\nNone of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c68bec0cb7169b21d20277b13cb52aaaf4487e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. This completes the proof.\n</p><p><br />\nThe answer to the problem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~G2JFForever\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Equation_Algorithm.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Equation_Algorithm)\">Solution 3 (Equation Algorithm)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Equation Algorithm)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is intuitively obvious, even to the most casual observer that the problem statement can be rewritten as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/77310564cd1b402862d18d9064b6ea427357432b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^4A + 10^4B + 10^3B + 10^3C + 10^2B + 10^2A + 10C + 10D + B + A = 10^4D + 10^3B + 10^2D + 10D + D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"821\" height=\"18\" />. This equation can be simplified into:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/493b3305e2eaf870a131bc14b38bfab5810d31e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^4A + 10^4B + 10^3C + 10^2B + 10^2A + 10C + B + A = 10^4D + 10^2D + D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"584\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now from here, it should hopefully make sense that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e43500b896047669fb9ba96ec80447ced28011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B = D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> by looking at the one's digit of both equations. Factoring out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/939c1f1501e50d9e0e1b26bfcd1ac06c69389921.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^4(A+B) + 10^3C + 10^2(A+B) + 10C + (B + A) = 10^4D + 10^2D + D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"575\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Which equals:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e93a8727a7b22cdc92e8157ba053bab5466cc40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^4(D) + 10^3C + 10^2(D) + 10C + D = 10^4D + 10^2D + D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"456\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>This simplifies into:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eecc654a285eeab94088a24a89088a37577e727c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^3C + 10C = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85aac914361efb48aaa13187304c1c5bdfef0589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e43500b896047669fb9ba96ec80447ced28011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B = D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f06f430accb7a96c4f93bc00d5dd27349e3fec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> or else there would be parts carried over in the equation. The positive integers that satisfy this equation are a minimum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a25c234892fb8a7738bc31e5ccee3bf9ad5afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and a maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b148ef6cc1c0ce3aebeede22fd06969a213bd5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/5436357ac86df88ed75b0b5217beb7ce85582ccc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767753d4fc32a9eb59711253d95324ed538a1540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$, 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/5/6750d3610b8426d83be272f82df161bc67fedff0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f6447e3134784b7a0594d2729d26b5c7733176fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$, 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/d/88dff7dbc4889a70738e683b568407cf2c5ea7f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$, 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e31c36d5fc1d81efa228343972e2b6e77d7739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$, 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/091f0f0b1d89a7e163f6d6597f1d6de31558d991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />. Giving \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0dc42f28c8ea4251496a9070b5715cf4ef7bf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~PeterDoesPhysics\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B\">2014 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AM